  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">UNDP has been identified in 2021 by the Haiti Country Coordinating Mechanism (CCM) and the Global Fund as the interim Principal Recipient for the Haiti malaria grant ($16,777,027) plus an additional emergency funding ($ 967,403). The overall goal is to eliminate malaria by 2025 with local malaria transmission reduced to 0 by: a.	confirming 100% of all malaria cases via Rapid Diagnostic Testing (RDT) or microscopy and, b.	correctly treating 100% of positive cases according to the national proto</narrative>
  </description>
