   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">Malaria I-5.1 Pr&#xe9;valence parasitaire : proportion de la population pr&#xe9;sentant une infection palustre</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">Les enqu&#xea;tes Trac seront  men&#xe9;es en 2024 et 2026 (2eme trimestre) et les  rapports seront disponibles respectivement les 1er mars 2025 et 2027.
Selon les estimations du Programme, en 2026, le taux de prevalence de la Malaria devrait chuter par rapport aux differentes strategies envisagees par le Programme.&quot;</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="1" year="2021"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="0"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">1.1 Malaria I-10??? Annual parasite incidence: Confirmed malaria cases (microscopy or RDT): rate per 1000 persons per year (Elimination settings)</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">&quot;Target assumptions: a) Confirmed malaria case definition: Haiti is in elimination phase, therefore, a confirmed case is defined as any case in which, regardless of the presence or absence of clinical symptoms, malaria parasites have been confirmed by quality-controlled laboratory diagnosis; b) the targets reflect the expected progressive reducton of the malaria incidence during 2021-2023 to achieve malaria elimination target or 0 indigenous cases notified by 2025 according to the NSP 2020-2025. To assess the burden of malaria in the general population in this elimination setting, the targets have been linked to a comprehensive and up-to-date analysis of the epidemiological situation, including size estimates of population sub-groups considered to be most at risk. The incidence rate targets correspond to:
2021: 6,191 / 12,156,738
2022: 3515 / 8,132,649
2023: 1304 / 6,992,234

Population at risk: The national malaria program has defined population at risk as the estimated population living in geographic areas classified as strata 2, 3 and 4 as per the 2019 updated national stratification. The stratification and population estimations were conducted as a national exercise led  by the National malaria program and the national department of epidemiologic surveillance (DELR) with support from the main stakeholders (PAHO and CHAI).

Measurement methods: The PR will report numerator and denominator based on the latest update available of the malaria transmission risk analysis and stratification conducted by the national program. However, if the risk analysis has not been updated by the reporting date, the PR will report using the denominator as per PF. The burden of malaria will be regularly monitored and the targets could be reviewed based on the collected evidences.&quot;</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="1" year="2021"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="0"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">Malaria I-3.1 D&#xe9;c&#xe8;s dus au paludisme : taux pour 100 000 personnes par an</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">Hypoth&#xe9;ses: Le Programme envisage une r&#xe9;duction de 66% du taux de mortalite&#xe9; en 2024 et 100% en 2025 et 2026. Le programme est align&#xe9; sur l&apos;objectif mondial de 0 d&#xe9;c&#xe8;s en 2028.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="6" year="2021"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="4"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
